WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.290 --> 00:00:05.649
What is spin? It’s something that apparently
some particles have that you can measure...

00:00:05.649 --> 00:00:07.810
but what is it?

00:00:07.810 --> 00:00:13.000
In the video I’ll explain how we know spin
exists, but also why we don’t understand

00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:14.490
it.

00:00:14.490 --> 00:00:19.040
Spin was a latecomer to the quantum mechanics
party. Even after Schrodinger wrote his famous

00:00:19.040 --> 00:00:24.820
equation, and everything seemed to be working
people didn’t realise it existed. Then people

00:00:24.820 --> 00:00:30.360
realised that some particles seem to have
odd magnetic properties the original quantum

00:00:30.360 --> 00:00:35.910
mechanics didn’t predict, and the source
of that was labeled spin.

00:00:35.910 --> 00:00:41.680
To understand this we’re going to need one
piece of classical electromagnetism theory:

00:00:41.680 --> 00:00:47.960
Whenever a charged particle moves, it creates
a magnetic field. This is pretty amazing,

00:00:47.960 --> 00:00:53.600
and you can see it for yourself, by putting
a compass next to a charge carrying wire.

00:00:53.600 --> 00:00:58.870
In fact, if you have charged particles going
in a small loop, this not only creates a magnetic

00:00:58.870 --> 00:01:05.830
field, that field pretty much looks like it’s
from a bar magnet. So then, we expect charged

00:01:05.830 --> 00:01:11.080
particles moving around, in circles, to act
as little magnets. Since that’s something

00:01:11.080 --> 00:01:16.680
we know from classical physics it was built
into quantum mechanics too from the start.

00:01:16.680 --> 00:01:21.400
But eventually some experiments showed that
there must be another source of magnetism.

00:01:21.400 --> 00:01:27.230
I’m going to explain one of those, a simplified
version of the stern-gerlach experiment.

00:01:27.230 --> 00:01:32.190
Let’s say we have a bunch of electrons by
themselves. They are charged, but they’re

00:01:32.190 --> 00:01:37.010
not doing little loops, so they shouldn’t
be magnets. We test this by putting them in

00:01:37.010 --> 00:01:38.659
a Stern-Gerlach apparatus.

00:01:38.659 --> 00:01:44.110
I’m not going to explain how the machine
works, but what is does is this. If a small

00:01:44.110 --> 00:01:50.040
magnet is placed inside it measures it’s
orientation. If the magnets North pole is

00:01:50.040 --> 00:01:55.951
up, it exerts an upward force on the magnet.
If the magnet is the other way around, it

00:01:55.951 --> 00:02:02.170
exerts a downward force. Of course there are
other orientations. If the magnet is like

00:02:02.170 --> 00:02:07.490
this, the magnet is still somewhat pointing
up, so the force is still up, but it’s smaller.

00:02:07.490 --> 00:02:12.529
It is proportional to how much this magnet
is pointing in the up direction. Similarly

00:02:12.529 --> 00:02:19.879
for this magnet pointing down. Say a magnet
is on its side, then it has no force at all.

00:02:19.879 --> 00:02:25.029
But these aren’t the only ways the magnet
can be oriented. It could be forward or backward

00:02:25.029 --> 00:02:31.739
or left or right, or any combination, so what
happens there? Well, this machine only measures

00:02:31.739 --> 00:02:37.370
how much the magnet is up or down. If the
magnet is like this, it’s pointing a bit

00:02:37.370 --> 00:02:42.989
upward. On the other hand, if a magnet was
just pointing left or right or forward or

00:02:42.989 --> 00:02:48.870
backward, it wouldn’t feel any force and
so it would go straight. So what expect is,

00:02:48.870 --> 00:02:54.489
if we shot through a bunch of magnets in random
orientations, they all land between here and

00:02:54.489 --> 00:02:57.340
here and in a pretty smooth distribution.

00:02:57.340 --> 00:03:03.890
Of course, if we threw in a non magnet, it
wouldn’t feel anything, and just go through.

00:03:03.890 --> 00:03:07.480
So that’s what we should expect with electrons.

00:03:07.480 --> 00:03:13.439
But we do the experiment and find something
really odd. The electrons do experience forces

00:03:13.439 --> 00:03:18.900
as if they’re magnets, but they don’t
spread out smoothly either. half of them go

00:03:18.900 --> 00:03:23.819
up to the same height, and the other half
go down, again, to the same height.

00:03:23.819 --> 00:03:30.129
Let’s look at this second mystery first.
If electrons really are magnets, we expect

00:03:30.129 --> 00:03:35.519
they’re randomly oriented, but these results
would be like saying that for some reason,

00:03:35.519 --> 00:03:43.029
half of them where pointing exactly up and
half exactly down. Well, maybe we did something

00:03:43.029 --> 00:03:48.739
very wrong when we prepared them that meant
this happened. So to test that, let’s do

00:03:48.739 --> 00:03:54.580
something clever. Let’s turn the stern gerlach
machine on its side. What that does is, now

00:03:54.580 --> 00:03:59.579
the machine measures how much the magnet is
pointing to the left or the right, instead

00:03:59.579 --> 00:04:05.470
of up and down. The more to the left a magnet
is pointing, the more to the left it goes.

00:04:05.470 --> 00:04:10.189
If a magnet isn’t pointing either left or
right, it just goes through.

00:04:10.189 --> 00:04:14.291
Now let’s use the same source of electrons
we had before. We think that they’re all

00:04:14.291 --> 00:04:19.310
pointing up or down, so if they go through
this machine, they shouldn’t be deflected

00:04:19.310 --> 00:04:23.380
at all.
What happens? Half of them go right, half

00:04:23.380 --> 00:04:30.910
of them go left. So then were they actually
oriented left and right all along? But that

00:04:30.910 --> 00:04:32.650
can’t be right either.

00:04:32.650 --> 00:04:36.810
Let me explain how to think of this in the
framework we built up in the last couple of

00:04:36.810 --> 00:04:38.190
videos.

00:04:38.190 --> 00:04:44.160
I can measure the up or downness of a particle,
so that is an observable. What are it’s

00:04:44.160 --> 00:04:48.630
eigenstates? Well, this experiment showed
that the particle can only be fully up or

00:04:48.630 --> 00:04:54.410
fully down, and nothing in between, so there
are only two eigenstates. We’ll call them

00:04:54.410 --> 00:05:00.480
spin up and spin down. Now we can apply the
quantum mechanical principle that, to fully

00:05:00.480 --> 00:05:06.200
describe the wavefunction of this particle,
we only need to describe it in one basis,

00:05:06.200 --> 00:05:12.430
so I can fully write the state of this particle
in terms of up and down. This is weird, because

00:05:12.430 --> 00:05:17.420
in classical physics this wouldn’t be enough
to tell you the state of a magnet. I can’t

00:05:17.420 --> 00:05:21.870
just tell you how much it’s pointing up
or down, I need to also tell you how left

00:05:21.870 --> 00:05:26.980
or right it is, and also how forward or backward.
But in quantum mechanics, this is enough.

00:05:26.980 --> 00:05:32.710
Let’s see what happens when we do some arbitrary
combination. Here, since the square of this

00:05:32.710 --> 00:05:38.640
number is bigger, it has a bigger chance of
being spin down, but still can be spin up.

00:05:38.640 --> 00:05:44.130
It doesn’t go ¾ of the way down ever though,
it’s only ever up or down.

00:05:44.130 --> 00:05:49.670
But what about if I flipped the machine on
it’s side to measure left rightness?

00:05:49.670 --> 00:05:54.930
In Quantum mechanics, if you tell me the wavefunction
in terms of up and down, I should be able

00:05:54.930 --> 00:05:59.690
to figure out what the wavefunction is in
terms of left and right. To be able to do

00:05:59.690 --> 00:06:05.931
that, we just need to know how to convert
up and down to left and right, but how? The

00:06:05.931 --> 00:06:12.320
coefficents should be equal in size, if we
use the classical analogy. A particle that’s

00:06:12.320 --> 00:06:17.830
fully up can’t be pointing either left or
right at all. A quantum particle that’s

00:06:17.830 --> 00:06:23.150
up, but is being measured for left and rightness
must go one way or the other, but at least,

00:06:23.150 --> 00:06:26.520
it shouldn’t be biased towards one side.

00:06:26.520 --> 00:06:31.520
Now we just need to decide the sign of each
of these. If we agree to call this way right

00:06:31.520 --> 00:06:36.620
and that left, then this turns out to be the
right way to do it.

00:06:36.620 --> 00:06:40.730
And this is something you’ll recognise from
the last two videos.

00:06:40.730 --> 00:06:45.590
Ok, so now I’ve shown you how quantum mechanics
deals with spin, let’s return to the must

00:06:45.590 --> 00:06:51.620
more difficult question, ‘what is spin?’
The electrons aren’t doing little loops,

00:06:51.620 --> 00:06:57.520
so why are they magnetic? This is what was
originally proposed: the electrons are spinning

00:06:57.520 --> 00:07:02.870
on their own axis. The idea is, if you have
a charged ball that’s spinning, that means

00:07:02.870 --> 00:07:08.440
bits of charge are moving in a circle, and
so it creates a magnetic field like a bar

00:07:08.440 --> 00:07:14.460
magnet. But we know this is wrong. If this
really was true, we can calculate how large

00:07:14.460 --> 00:07:20.090
the electron should be- it’s bigger than
the whole atom. It also makes some other incorrect

00:07:20.090 --> 00:07:25.270
conclusions. These days we think the electron
isn’t a ball, it’s an infinitely small

00:07:25.270 --> 00:07:27.610
point- and that can’t spin.

00:07:27.610 --> 00:07:33.620
I think this image of the electron spinning,
is really more harmful than helpful- not just

00:07:33.620 --> 00:07:39.250
because it makes all kinds of incorrect predictions,
but because feeling like we understand something

00:07:39.250 --> 00:07:44.360
stops us from asking about what it is. But,
making this video I realised there’s lots

00:07:44.360 --> 00:07:49.700
of other physics terms I don’t understand.
What is energy? What’s charge? It seems

00:07:49.700 --> 00:07:54.980
like we define those things by how we measure
them, and then same is true for spin, spin

00:07:54.980 --> 00:07:59.431
is that thing that makes some particles act
a bit like magnets. I really hope that, in

00:07:59.431 --> 00:08:04.120
the future as we understand more physics,
more of these terms can be understood in terms

00:08:04.120 --> 00:08:10.330
of deeper physics. There is some hope for
spin. I told you that spin had to be added

00:08:10.330 --> 00:08:15.780
to quantum mechanics in an ad hoc way. This
is true, but when Dirac tried to merge standard

00:08:15.780 --> 00:08:21.940
quantum mechanics and relativity, something
in his new equation acted a lot like spin.

00:08:21.940 --> 00:08:26.990
While this was awesome, I don’t feel like
it solves the mystery of spin, because while

00:08:26.990 --> 00:08:32.270
it comes out of the maths, it still doesn’t
explain what it is, or why relativity demands

00:08:32.270 --> 00:08:38.120
it exists. Maybe there are some properties
of physics we can never understand, and maybe

00:08:38.120 --> 00:08:40.279
spin is one of them.

00:08:40.279 --> 00:08:45.959
There was so much more I could have said about
spin but I ran way over time. So, I thought

00:08:45.959 --> 00:08:49.620
it would be fun if you guys taught each other
instead, so I’ll set this as homework.

00:08:49.620 --> 00:08:53.600
In the description, I’ve put a whole lot
of questions I didn’t answer in the video.

00:08:53.600 --> 00:08:58.740
I would love if you picked one of more of
these, or found your own and did some research.

00:08:58.740 --> 00:09:03.180
You can present your work in any format you
want: as a Youtube comment, on any of these

00:09:03.180 --> 00:09:08.870
social media accounts, on your own website
etc. It would be kind of amazing if you want

00:09:08.870 --> 00:09:12.399
to make it into a video, but I know that’s
daunting.

00:09:12.399 --> 00:09:16.370
As for the content, you should know that some
of the questions I asked in the description

00:09:16.370 --> 00:09:22.630
are ones I don’t know the answer to despite
trying to find out, so it’s absolutely fine

00:09:22.630 --> 00:09:28.240
to just make an attempt- this doesn’t have
to be a huge thing. Also, a lot of sources

00:09:28.240 --> 00:09:35.430
claim to answer questions but leave big gaps,
or make potentially unjustified assumptions.

00:09:35.430 --> 00:09:41.139
And some of these questions are still unanswered,
even though there are some interesting leads.

00:09:41.139 --> 00:09:47.160
So then your task isn’t to necessarily definitively
answer your question. In fact, I’d way rather

00:09:47.160 --> 00:09:53.259
you point out why you don’t understand something,
or discuss several possible solutions. Don’t

00:09:53.259 --> 00:09:59.480
worry about being dumb. Not knowing things
isn’t dumb, pretending you know things is

00:09:59.480 --> 00:10:00.480
dumb.

00:10:00.480 --> 00:10:05.360
I’d love if you read each other’s responses.
If you want to give any constructive feedback

00:10:05.360 --> 00:10:11.459
and start a discussion, then awesome I’m
encourage that so much- but remember be kind.

00:10:11.459 --> 00:10:15.940
Anyway, good luck, I’m really looking forward
to learning things from you!

